Your five questions rest on three ideas, so here's the map:

- **Backside attack and crowding** (Q1, Q3, Q5): SN2 needs the nucleophile to approach the carbon from the side opposite the leaving group.
- **Leaving group ability** (Q2): what makes a group willing to leave with the electron pair.
- **Solvent effects on the nucleophile** (Q4).

Work through the practice set below. Write your answer to each question in your own words, including the reasoning, since that's what a professor's exam will ask for. The hint button gives a parallel case, never your actual question. When you're done, send your answers and I'll give a verdict on each.

```show_widget
<div id="app" style="font-family:system-ui,sans-serif;max-width:560px;padding:4px">
  <div style="display:flex;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center;margin-bottom:8px">
    <strong id="hdr"></strong>
    <span id="dots" style="letter-spacing:3px"></span>
  </div>
  <div id="q" style="margin-bottom:8px;line-height:1.4"></div>
  <textarea id="ans" rows="4" style="width:100%;box-sizing:border-box;padding:8px;font:inherit;border:1px solid currentColor;border-radius:6px;background:transparent;color:inherit" placeholder="Your answer and your reasoning..."></textarea>
  <div id="hint" style="margin:8px 0;padding:8px;border-left:3px solid currentColor;opacity:.85;display:none;line-height:1.4"></div>
  <div style="display:flex;gap:8px;flex-wrap:wrap;margin-top:8px">
    <button id="hb">Hint (parallel case)</button>
    <button id="pb">Back</button>
    <button id="nb">Next</button>
    <button id="sb" style="font-weight:600">Send my answers</button>
  </div>
</div>
<script>
const Q=[
 "Rank by SN2 rate (fastest to slowest): 1-bromobutane, 2-bromobutane, 2-bromo-2-methylpropane.",
 "Which is the better leaving group, Cl- or I-? Why?",
 "Predict the product of sodium ethoxide with iodomethane.",
 "Why does DMSO speed up SN2 compared with methanol?",
 "What happens to the stereocenter in (R)-2-bromobutane with NaCN?"];
const H=[
 ["Parallel: rank chloromethane, chloroethane, 2-chloropropane for SN2. Picture the nucleophile coming in opposite the Cl. What sits near that path?","Count the groups attached to the carbon bearing the halogen in each case."],
 ["Parallel: compare Br- with F-. Look up the pKa of HBr vs HF. How does the stability of the departing anion relate to that?","Think about size and how well each anion spreads out its negative charge."],
 ["Parallel: hydroxide + chloromethane. Identify the nucleophile, the electrophilic carbon and what leaves.","Now do the same bookkeeping with ethoxide as the nucleophile and iodide as the leaving group."],
 ["Parallel: how does methanol's O-H interact with an anion like acetate? Compare that with how DMSO (no O-H) interacts with the cation.","Ask which solvent leaves the anionic nucleophile freer to attack, and why."],
 ["Parallel: (S)-2-chloropentane + hydroxide by SN2. Draw the carbon with the nucleophile entering opposite Cl.","Think of an umbrella flipping inside out in wind. What happens to the three other groups? Then check the CIP priorities before naming R or S."]];
let i=0,a=["","","","",""],h=[0,0,0,0,0];
const $=id=>document.getElementById(id);
function r(){
 $('hdr').textContent="Question "+(i+1)+" of 5";
 $('q').textContent=Q[i];
 $('ans').value=a[i];
 $('dots').textContent=a.map((x,k)=>x.trim()?(k==i?"◉":"●"):(k==i?"◎":"○")).join("");
 const hh=$('hint');
 if(h[i]>0){hh.style.display='block';hh.textContent=H[i].slice(0,h[i]).join("  ")}else hh.style.display='none';
 $('hb').disabled=h[i]>=2;$('pb').disabled=i==0;$('nb').disabled=i==4;
}
$('ans').oninput=e=>{a[i]=e.target.value;$('dots').textContent=a.map((x,k)=>x.trim()?(k==i?"◉":"●"):(k==i?"◎":"○")).join("")};
$('hb').onclick=()=>{h[i]++;r()};
$('pb').onclick=()=>{i--;r()};
$('nb').onclick=()=>{i++;r()};
$('sb').onclick=()=>{
 let t="Here are my answers to the SN2 practice set (hints used: "+h.join(",")+").\n";
 a.forEach((x,k)=>{t+=(k+1)+". "+(x.trim()||"(no answer yet)")+"\n"});
 t+="Give me a verdict on each (right, not yet, or partly right) and tell me which gap to fix first.";
 sendPrompt(t);
};
r();
</script>
```

Answer all five if you can, even with a guess. A wrong guess you commit to teaches more than a blank. If a question stumps you completely, write what you do know about it, and I'll build from there.
